#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:1
msgid "Path-to-RegExp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:3
msgid ""
"Turn an Express-style path string such as `/user/:name` into a regular "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:5
msgid "**Note:** This is a legacy branch. You should upgrade to `1.x`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:7
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:13
msgid "pathToRegexp(path, keys, options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:15
msgid ""
"**path** A string in the express format, an array of such strings, or a "
"regular expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:16
msgid ""
"**keys** An array to be populated with the keys present in the url.  Once"
" the function completes, this will be an array of strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:17
msgid "**options**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:18
msgid ""
"**options.sensitive** Defaults to false, set this to true to make routes "
"case sensitive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:19
msgid ""
"**options.strict** Defaults to false, set this to true to make the "
"trailing slash matter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:20
msgid ""
"**options.end** Defaults to true, set this to false to only match the "
"prefix of the URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:29
msgid "Live Demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-to-regexp_Readme.md:31
msgid ""
"You can see a live demo of this library in use at [express-route-"
"tester](http://forbeslindesay.github.com/express-route-tester/)."
msgstr ""

